Z||000000||turbo86se||11-20-2001||11:20 PM||||I remember reading a post on this not too long ago, and I'm looking for info. <BR>I believe you can do it to the sunroof or to the front frame, under the hood.<BR>I'd like to do this to both my Fieros, neither has a sunroof. One is a plain roof and one is a T-Top.<P>I'm looking for help to wire it to the frame. My goal is to get rid of the ugly antenna and pick up a killer radio station an hour away. There's only one good radio station around here, and I'm tired of their 20 minute music free marathons. Two songs then 20 minutes of commercials.<P>Thanks! Hey cool 800th post in over two years!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SC.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||fropuff||11-21-2001||12:06 AM||||I believe it was Smoooooth that did the antenna under the front hood thing.  I want to pick up a station three hours away, but I don't know if this way would do it.  Try a search for Smoooooth.  Good luck.  Hope you can figure it out.  Keep us updated.  Bye!||||reg||1
Z||000002||Smoooooth GT||11-21-2001||12:35 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by turbo86se:<BR><B>I remember reading a post on this not too long ago, and I'm looking for info. <BR>I believe you can do it to the sunroof or to the front frame, under the hood.<BR>I'd like to do this to both my Fieros, neither has a sunroof. One is a plain roof and one is a T-Top.<P>I'm looking for help to wire it to the frame. My goal is to get rid of the ugly antenna and pick up a killer radio station an hour away. There's only one good radio station around here, and I'm tired of their 20 minute music free marathons. Two songs then 20 minutes of commercials.<P>Thanks! Hey cool 800th post in over two years!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It was me... Yes, I justed wrapped heavy gauge speaker wire around it tightly and ran it under the front trunk section a few times!!! I can get channel's outta Dallas and that's 110 miles from me.... Steve<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/texas_1.gif">          <BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||11-21-2001||05:46 AM||||I ran one of the self adhesive antenna wires across the top and sides of winshield under the side trim and front edge of headliner. I get strong stations like from 50 miles. $5 at Radio Shack.||||reg||1
